WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.184 --> 00:00:03.351
(upbeat guitar music)

00:00:04.550 --> 00:00:06.950
- This menorah is a real Texas menorah.

00:00:06.950 --> 00:00:08.840
Most people who know much about menorahs

00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:11.510
don't know anything about armadillos.

00:00:11.510 --> 00:00:13.700
And the people who do
know about armadillos

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:16.972
certainly don't know
anything about menorahs.

00:00:17.322 --> 00:00:20.240
So it's very unusual to
find people like myself

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:22.890
that know about menorahs and armadillos.

00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:25.570
- I'm Nico Tortorella.

00:00:25.570 --> 00:00:28.450
I'm an actor, an activist
and a firm believer that

00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:31.230
our differences actually make us stronger.

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:33.820
I'm on a journey with
IKEA to meet real people

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:37.020
and discover the diverse
and spectacular ways

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:38.453
they celebrate the holidays.

00:00:41.650 --> 00:00:43.040
Maybe you celebrate the holidays

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:45.730
with traditional food and decorations;

00:00:45.730 --> 00:00:48.530
or, maybe you celebrate
them with your bandmates

00:00:48.530 --> 00:00:50.290
and a guitar in hand,

00:00:50.290 --> 00:00:53.030
like country music legend Kinky Friedman.

00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:56.199
- Hi, this is Kinky
Friedman, and I write songs.

00:00:56.199 --> 00:00:58.280
(melancholy acoustic guitar)

00:00:58.280 --> 00:00:59.113
- [Nico] What would you say

00:00:59.113 --> 00:01:01.300
your greatest achievement has been?

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:02.740
- Well, playing the Grand Ole Opry.

00:01:02.740 --> 00:01:03.691
- Oh, yeah?

00:01:03.691 --> 00:01:05.450
What year was that?

00:01:05.450 --> 00:01:06.713
- '73.

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:11.470
And, um, that's where I was introduced as

00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:13.580
the first full-blooded Jew to ever appear

00:01:13.580 --> 00:01:15.120
on the Grand Ole Opry stage.
- Wow.

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:16.895
- Yeah,I loved it.

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:21.360
Years later I discover that
Nelson Mandela had smuggled

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:24.790
tape cassettes in his
prison cell in Robben Island

00:01:24.790 --> 00:01:28.000
and one of them was Sold
American, my record.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:31.970
I never dreamed that Nelson
Mandela would be listening.

00:01:31.970 --> 00:01:33.300
- Kinky celebrates the holidays

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:35.550
in a very non-traditional way.

00:01:35.550 --> 00:01:37.420
He gets his chosen family together:

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:40.730
his bandmates, people in
his community, his friends.

00:01:40.730 --> 00:01:43.107
They get together, and they play music.

00:01:43.107 --> 00:01:44.727
(laughing)

00:01:44.727 --> 00:01:48.394
♪ Nagila hava, nagila hava. ♪

00:01:49.703 --> 00:01:51.830
Kinky's Jewishness made him stand out,

00:01:51.830 --> 00:01:55.480
gave him this real powerful
angle to write from.

00:01:55.480 --> 00:02:00.253
He uses this common bond of
music to spread tradition.

00:02:01.353 --> 00:02:05.020
- An important thing
about being Jewish is that

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:07.623
you are definitely on
the outside looking in.

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:10.940
But that's where the
best material comes from,

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:14.500
if you're an author of
any kind or a songwriter

00:02:15.670 --> 00:02:17.460
or just a human being.

00:02:17.460 --> 00:02:20.110
That's where you more clearly

00:02:21.490 --> 00:02:23.939
see what life is all about.

00:02:23.939 --> 00:02:28.939
♪ Well, the only whole
heart is a broken one. ♪

00:02:30.039 --> 00:02:34.723
♪ And the only true
love an unspoken one. ♪

00:02:34.723 --> 00:02:36.209
One, two, three.
- One, two, three.

00:02:36.209 --> 00:02:38.209
(howls)

00:02:39.825 --> 00:02:40.658
Wow.

00:02:41.735 --> 00:02:44.360
(upbeat acoustic guitar)

00:02:44.360 --> 00:02:48.058
In years past, Kinky has
embarked on Hanukkah tours.

00:02:48.908 --> 00:02:50.568
This year, we had a small concert

00:02:50.568 --> 00:02:52.089
with some locals at the ranch.

00:02:52.089 --> 00:02:54.791
♪ - That I used to know. ♪

00:02:54.791 --> 00:02:59.791
♪ Now it's me and a three-legged
dog named Freedom. ♪

00:03:00.305 --> 00:03:04.901
- As unique as Kinky is, his
interpretation of Hanukkah

00:03:04.901 --> 00:03:07.110
is as pure as gold.

00:03:07.110 --> 00:03:09.870
And maybe he doesn't celebrate
it the way you see on TV.

00:03:09.870 --> 00:03:11.490
Maybe those are the things

00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:14.561
that make his tradition so special.

00:03:14.561 --> 00:03:18.778
♪ -There ain't no quit
in either one of us. ♪

00:03:18.778 --> 00:03:21.228
(defiant acoustic guitar)

00:03:21.228 --> 00:03:23.978
(crowd applauds)

